        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1a5aa842-88df-320e-9521-409cd58fa32d",
                "word": "rondtoeren",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "177f412f-43ca-35b4-a89e-4c0c3357cca1",
                        "entry_id": "1a5aa842-88df-320e-9521-409cd58fa32d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ongericht rondrijden"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0d27d98-cc09-4819-8829-97920330f7d7",
                                "sense_id": "177f412f-43ca-35b4-a89e-4c0c3357cca1",
                                "text": "Maar toen zei ze toch iets: ‘Vind je het goed dat we gewoon gaan slapen en morgen dingen bespreken, als ik klaar ben met werken? We kunnen- je mag vast Marcies auto wel lenen, denk ik, als je een beetje wilt rondtoeren of zo."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c46aeca7-9b8d-4461-89a6-e7fae3d4955f",
                                "sense_id": "177f412f-43ca-35b4-a89e-4c0c3357cca1",
                                "text": "Nou ja, kennen. Natuurlijk wisten de dorpsbewoners wel wie Jasper S. was. En hij begaf zich ook weleens onder de mensen, bijvoorbeeld bij vergaderingen van de boerenvereniging uit Oudwoude. Maar een goed inzicht in het karakter van de veehouder, dat hebben hoogstwaarschijnlijk niet veel dorpsbewoners gehad. Het is op z'n zachtst gezegd geen extraverte man. Natuurlijk, er was dat akkefietje met de gestolen auto van een buur, waarmee hij ging rondtoeren."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "563cb8ef-fd68-4cb9-8db8-049dde28a523",
                        "source_entry_id": "1a5aa842-88df-320e-9521-409cd58fa32d",
                        "source_sense_id": "177f412f-43ca-35b4-a89e-4c0c3357cca1",
                        "source_sense_description": "ongericht rondrijden",
                        "target_lang_word": "tootle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tootle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df44ef35-c099-3aad-9875-4e32d2c80053",
                                        "entry_id": "cac0a5d6-6596-3a6d-8387-74f3d74d2fb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a soft toot sound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09b0160b-de2d-4675-b28e-aee62a91e21c",
                                                "sense_id": "df44ef35-c099-3aad-9875-4e32d2c80053",
                                                "text": "Now the scythe the morn salutes,\nIn the meadow tinkling soon;\nWhile on mellow-tootling flutes\nSweetly breathes the shepherd’s tune."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b68c8a0-f16f-4845-a1d2-3a119daa09f0",
                                                "sense_id": "df44ef35-c099-3aad-9875-4e32d2c80053",
                                                "text": "We know the old lady is upstairs and that she is quite alone in the house and therefore it would be perfectly useless for her to tootle on her bedroom bell."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "821aa3ce-fdd2-4529-a629-92fd2bda4b14",
                                                "sense_id": "df44ef35-c099-3aad-9875-4e32d2c80053",
                                                "text": "Their booth did not have so many customers as did the other booths where the tootling laugh of Maybelle Merriwether sounded and Fanny Elsing’s giggles and the Whiting girls’ repartee made merriment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "168807ff-d6e8-4145-872d-939a9050dec7",
                                                "sense_id": "df44ef35-c099-3aad-9875-4e32d2c80053",
                                                "text": "During the night, some of the locomotives began to tootle to one another, and then to move."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8139952-66d4-3081-9cf5-9f75171a0a97",
                                        "entry_id": "cac0a5d6-6596-3a6d-8387-74f3d74d2fb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play (a musical instrument) making such a sound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "425831b0-5a6e-4ff1-b8f9-ee20eb8d28c8",
                                                "sense_id": "c8139952-66d4-3081-9cf5-9f75171a0a97",
                                                "text": "A young, fresh-faced man, sitting by the driver, tootled a tandem horn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef3a47c8-27df-446d-b541-14382fcdc1e8",
                                                "sense_id": "c8139952-66d4-3081-9cf5-9f75171a0a97",
                                                "text": "[…] Cecil can tootle a pretty fair sax, at that, if the play happens to come up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9254fd0d-d89c-3d48-84a2-83aa4b926596",
                                        "entry_id": "cac0a5d6-6596-3a6d-8387-74f3d74d2fb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To go (somewhere); to amble aimlessly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80a50a08-e3da-488d-a6ae-334ba3c02640",
                                                "sense_id": "9254fd0d-d89c-3d48-84a2-83aa4b926596",
                                                "text": "I suppose we’d better tootle back to the ballroom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "100f1287-f48e-4837-b35a-287331f0dd63",
                                                "sense_id": "9254fd0d-d89c-3d48-84a2-83aa4b926596",
                                                "text": "‘When my old bike comes I shall tootle up and down the drive! Some swank!’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7009dc1e-43d4-4b8c-9c30-851fb30b77b0",
                                                "sense_id": "9254fd0d-d89c-3d48-84a2-83aa4b926596",
                                                "text": "I was about to go, I thought I’d tootle down to the Coleherne perhaps, then I wouldn’t be too far away if the bleep went."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7759d16b-de09-32be-9774-608cd4a044f7",
                                        "entry_id": "cac0a5d6-6596-3a6d-8387-74f3d74d2fb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To transport (someone somewhere)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d6c5a38-471b-439e-83fb-9d9f1d36c6fb",
                                                "sense_id": "7759d16b-de09-32be-9774-608cd4a044f7",
                                                "text": "[…] he would just see if his shover had enough in the tank to tootle them down to Warborough […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75dc1564-c727-4a9f-8304-412edbcd3365",
                                                "sense_id": "7759d16b-de09-32be-9774-608cd4a044f7",
                                                "text": "Say I pick you up and tootle you over with your hens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tootle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8f542c9-4b02-3224-a450-97ebce5beb98",
                                        "entry_id": "f3e959e2-6d52-3af4-9e1f-59f7f583c3d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A soft toot sound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6314d2fb-a078-4e2f-99ef-66e361ee5847",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f542c9-4b02-3224-a450-97ebce5beb98",
                                                "text": "1891, Thirteen Essays on Education, London: Percival & Co., E. W. Howson, “The Teaching of Music in Public Schools,” p. 37,\nNo one, least of all those with a musical ear, can take a form or even read a book in close proximity to the ineffectual tootle of a flute, the maddening squeaks of a raw fiddler, or the spasmodic grunts of a euphonium."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e1d51ed-18ac-40c5-af72-136ff89f8ad6",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f542c9-4b02-3224-a450-97ebce5beb98",
                                                "text": "The glamour of the sawdust world, the cheers of the crowd, the smell of hot dogs and cotton candy, the blare and tootle of the midway—he envied the gypsy family, here today and gone tomorrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d9d62da-d1ee-4b06-ba06-a0a2b6dfc517",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f542c9-4b02-3224-a450-97ebce5beb98",
                                                "text": "One blast [of the trumpet], and [the sheep] would go here, two and they would go there, some tootles and they would run up the hill, a high note and they would stop short […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ca88c35-7ff2-324b-a344-86c9c6536bef",
                                        "entry_id": "f3e959e2-6d52-3af4-9e1f-59f7f583c3d4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A trip or excursion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc80938b-6718-43a6-a0d7-82b569e14fcd",
                                                "sense_id": "9ca88c35-7ff2-324b-a344-86c9c6536bef",
                                                "text": "In between, is Granny May’s only daughter Juliet. A wonderful character who still joins me on the odd tootle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "819099e0-a735-4635-88d2-b323f30afa01",
                                                "sense_id": "9ca88c35-7ff2-324b-a344-86c9c6536bef",
                                                "text": "On weekends you can take a short tootle over to itsy-bitsy Pelican Island on a free ferry […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
